When doing tagseq, it is important to remember that the program Transdecoder can remove the Poly-A tail of the reference transcriptome, which will reduce the mapping rates of the tagseq reads. The main way to summarize the number of contigs is with CD-hit (which collapses contigs based on similarity).

Examples on how to run the scripts available at: https://github.com/z0on/tag-based_RNAseq/tree/master
The programs in PERL should be installed to your local supercomputer. 

